# Dependencies
node_modules/

# The mini-app installs against either the npm-published package or a tarball
# packed from this working tree (see the consumer-smoke CI job), so pinning its
# resolution is wrong — the committed lockfile used to reference a
# file:../../*.tgz that was never in the repo, which made a fresh clone
# un-installable.
examples/mini-app/pnpm-lock.yaml
.pnp.*
.yarn/

